// Depth 5 of the Stack, rolled rather than authored: whatever the game
// actually puts in front of a party that has descended five frames.
//
// This band was measured at 0/50 wins on 2026-08-08 and never fixed. That
// measurement used a fixture with no gear, which is not what a party four
// frames down looks like — a player who got there has been through four
// frames of caches and fights. So this one is geared and partied, to ask
// the narrower question: is depth 5 unwinnable for a party that arrived
// there in reasonable shape, or only for a naked one?
//
// `Stack` takes its own biome because the biome alone decides the species
// pool; the zone comes from the player row, since `ZoneLevel` drives both
// gear scaling and enemy scaling and two zones on one screen would be two
// answers to one question.
(
    player: Fresh(level: 20, zone: 3),
    equip: [
        (item: "plasma_router", tier: 0),
        (item: "bastion_lattice", tier: 0),
        (item: "singularity_matrix", tier: 0),
    ],
    party: [
        (species: "scrapper", level: 12),
        (species: "scrapper", level: 12),
        (species: "scrapper", level: 12),
    ],
    encounter: Some(Stack(biome: NullSector, depth: 5)),
    reps: 50,
    seed: 41,
)
